Focus loops with cwm, OpenBSD's default window manager, which activates a
client on every EnterNotify regardless of its mode and then sends
WM_TAKE_FOCUS:
- Proton's wait_grab_pointer() grabs and ungrabs the pointer, generating
  crossing events; only do it while a mouse button is pressed (window
  manager move/resize grabs need one).  Two windows otherwise took the
  focus from each other in a tight loop (_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW changing every
  millisecond; kernel32 console test children never exited).
- Ignore WM_TAKE_FOCUS when the window already is the foreground window
  and has the X input focus (idle programs kept explorer.exe and
  wineserver busy).

Index: dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
